Package: hd-qemu-kvm
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Erik Van Hamme <erik.vanhamme@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: python3, python3-debconf, debconf (>= 0.5) | debconf-2.0, hd-network,
 qemu-system-x86, qemu-utils, ovmf, libvirt-daemon-system, libvirt-clients, bridge-utils
Suggests: virt-manager
Conflicts: qemu-system-gui
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Description: HyprDebian Qemu/KVM support
 Installs Qemu with KVM, the UEFI firmware OVMF and libvirt, and sets them up
 to run virtual machines on the network through the bridge br0.
 .
 The first installation makes the wired interfaces that the administrator
 chooses ports of the bridge br0, with the network commands of hd-network.
 libvirtd only listens on its local sockets and stores secrets without
 encryption. The module br_netfilter is loaded with the traffic over bridges
 kept out of the firewall, and new users connect virsh and virt-manager to
 qemu:///system. Adding users to the groups libvirt and kvm is left to the
 administrator.
